throughout the Halloween franchise the  timeline diverges multiple times and the  main series even features one entry  without Michael Myers but we're here to  help sort through it all so grab your  favorite carving knife and let's dig in  this is Michael Myers backstory  explained the story of Michael Myers  begins on Halloween night in 1963 in the  Suburban town of Haddonfield Illinois as  six-year-old Michael gets up walks into  his sister's room and stabs her to death  Michael is sent to Smith's Grove  sanitarium where he spends the rest of  his childhood and Adolescence he has  observed and studied by Dr Sam Loomis  who winds up becoming an expert on the  man the myth the legend that is Michael  Myers  on October 30th 1978 the story of  Michael Myers begins in Earnest he  escapes from Smith's Grove the Night  Before Halloween and descends upon  Haddonfield meanwhile high schooler Lori  Strode played by Jamie Lee Curtis in her  first film role is preparing for a  boring Halloween night babysitting young  Tommy Doyle near the Mars home which is  now abandoned instead of having a dull  Knight earning a little money on the  side Lori ends up at the tail end of  Michael's Killing Spree after a night of  tracking Michael Loomis comes to the  house where Lori is fighting him off and  manages to put Six Bullets in the Killer  Halloween 2 picks up later that night  when Lori is brought to the Haddonfield  Memorial Hospital where Michael  reappears to finish what he started the  sequel begins what would become a major  expansion of the Halloween lore by  revealing that Lori is Michael's sister  according to Halloween 2 Lori was taken  in and raised by the strodes this  explains why Michael is so dead set on  killing Lori as he wants to finish what  he started Halloween 2 ends with Michael  being presumed dead when there's a fire  at the hospital  the third movie in the franchise  Halloween three Season of the Witch was  an experiment that tried to take the  franchise in an anthology Direction and  away from Michael Myers after lukewarm  reviews the series fell into limbo for  years after it returned with 1988's  Halloween for the return of Michael  Myers it never again strayed from the  unfeeling killer at its core Halloween 4  stars Danielle Harris as Jamie Lloyd  Lori strode's daughter Jaime is living  with a foster family and has recurring  dreams of Michael coming together those  dreams turn out to be warnings when  Michael wakes up from a 10-year coma and  goes after his closest living relative  the movie ends in a standoff near an  abandoned mine but only after depicting  a moment of psychic connection initially  established via physical contact with  Jaime in the final moments of Halloween  4 the family returns home Jamie eerily  wearing a similar costume to the one  Michael wore all the way back in 1963.  just whenever everyone thinks they're  safe Jaime attacks her foster mother and  reappears at the top of the stairs  holding a bloody pair of scissors Dr  Loomis tries to shoot her but is sorted  as Halloween 5 the Revenge of Michael  Myers begins Jaime is mute and in a  psychiatric hospital after attempting to  kill her foster mother this is implied  to be the result of a moment she shared  with Michael in the previous movie  sparking a connection that leaves Jaime  suffering hallucinations that keep her  bond with Michael shrouded in mystery in  the curse of Michael Myers Michael  returns to his childhood home to kill  the Strode family that now lives there  Tommy Doyle now an adult lives across  the street  my name's Tommy  I was only eight years old when I saw  him  Doyle has been studying Michael and has  discovered that the root of his evil is  an ancient Druid curse known as Thorne  this brings the family connection full  circle as the conditions of the curse  say The Afflicted must kill their next  of kin on Halloween night  made 20 years after the original  Halloween H2O 20 years later brought  Jamie Lee Curtis back for a story  pitched as a direct sequel to Halloween  2. this movie returns Michael's  motivations to the roots with him  specifically trying to find and kill  Laurie Strode H2O brings Michael from  Haddonfield to California where Lori has  built a new identity and life for  herself as a school teacher however he's  foiled again with what looks like the  most definitive Michael kill yet when  Lori Chomps off his head with a fire ax  in an unexpected turn Halloween  resurrection reveals that the ending of  H2O was an illusion of course the  decapitated man wasn't Michael instead  Lori killed an innocent man and now has  been institutionalized honey you come  for me sooner or later despite Lori's  best lead traps Michael breaks into the  sanitarium where she's being held she's  about to kill him but begins to Grapple  with his mask to make sure it's the real  Michael that doubt gives Michael enough  time to stab and finally kill Lori  tossing her off the roof and that's only  the beginning of Resurrection Michael  goes on yet another Killing Spree aided  in part by Busta Rhymes and Tyra Banks  Yes you heard that right Lori's death  could have been a huge moment in the  Halloween Cannon but it finally left the  franchise nowhere to go but back to the  beginning  in 2007 the franchise returned thanks to  Rob Zombie who directed a remake of the  original 1978 Carpenter Classic this  poorly received installment more or less  retold the story of the first movie but  many felt it didn't hold a candle to the  original zombie followed up his remake  with his own version of Halloween 2 set  two years after the events in  Haddonfield Lori begins having  hallucinations in which she sees herself  acting out Michael's past murders Laurie  manages to actually kill Michael after  stabbing him with his own knife Laurie  puts on his mask and becomes the new  Michael Myers  with the 2018 reimagining of Halloween  the series went back to basics giving  viewers a direct sequel to 1978's  Halloween and disregarding the big twist  connecting Lori and Michael in Halloween  2. in this timeline Michael has been  incarcerated for the past 40 years for  the killings he committed in the very  first movie he breaks out to track down  and kill Lori who in this continuity is  definitely not his sister over the years  Laurie has become a reclusive alcoholic  who's very good at setting traps for  Michael it pays off because a traps She  lays for him sets her house Ablaze with  Michael presumably dead inside but with  sequel's Halloween kills and Halloween  ends announced shortly after that  movie's release it was soon clear that  Michael also survived that fire and  lived to kill again check out one of our  newest videos right here plus even more  Looper videos about your favorite horror  movies are coming soon subscribe to our  YouTube channel and hit the Bell so you  don't miss a single one  [Music]
 

